54
00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:58.418
do you suggest?" Hugh demanded. "Whip me instead," Miles said. "I will take his lashes."

55
00:05:58.419 --> 00:06:07.085
Hugh's face lit up with satisfaction. He immediately gave orders for Miles to be whipped

56
00:06:07.086 --> 00:06:12.482
in public, before the crowd. "No, Miles!" Edward shouted. Crying, he ran to his friend.

57
00:06:12.483 --> 00:06:20.320
"Don't worry about me, Your Majesty," Miles said with a smile. "When this is over,

58
00:06:20.321 --> 00:06:28.886
we can get on with our plan." Miles didn't flinch as the whip came down. Edward

59
00:06:28.887 --> 00:06:36.878
turned away, unable to watch, tears streaming down his cheeks. Never before had anyone been

60
00:06:36.879 --> 00:06:45.882
so loyal and kind to him. He knew only one way to express his gratitude.

61
00:06:45.883 --> 00:06:51.300
"Your sacrifices are not impulsive or for selfish gain, but rather noble and loyal," Edward

62
00:06:51.301 --> 00:06:54.538
said quietly. "They have not gone unnoticed. You are no longer a knight." Miles' eyes

63
00:06:54.539 --> 00:07:08.881
widened in surprise. "I am raising your rank," Edward declared. "From this moment on, by

64
00:07:08.882 --> 00:07:15.689
the authority given me, you shall be known as the Earl of Kent, beloved and

65
00:07:15.690 --> 00:07:21.593
trusted servant of the king!" "I'm an earl?" Miles' eyes watered as Edward placed his

66
00:07:21.594 --> 00:07:25.360
hand on Miles' head. "Yes. You have saved the king from shame and suffering!" Edward

67
00:07:25.361 --> 00:07:34.837
told him. "Thank you, Your Majesty," Miles whispered. Now that it was all over, the

68
00:07:34.838 --> 00:07:44.499
crowd began to dwindle and the guards returned to the prison. Hugh left without a

69
00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:52.826
backward glance. Miles and Edward were alone. "We need to find a place to rest,"

70
00:07:52.827 --> 00:07:57.483
Edward said as Miles, weak from pain, leaned on the boy. But Miles shook his

71
00:07:57.484 --> 00:08:03.722
head. "No. The king's coronation is tomorrow," he said hoarsely. We must go." "Are you sure

72
00:08:03.723 --> 00:08:10.897
you are strong enough to make the journey?" Edward asked. Miles turned to look at

73
00:08:10.898 --> 00:08:16.063
him, touched. "The boy has changed," Miles thought. "He used to think only of himself,

74
00:08:16.064 --> 00:08:22.382
but now I see something else—he is worried about me." Miles smiled at Edward and

75
00:08:22.383 --> 00:08:26.390
said, "I'm sure, Your Majesty." Edward looked down for a moment, embarrassed. "Thank you for

76
00:08:26.391 --> 00:08:29.643
all that you have done for me." "You're welcome, Your Majesty," Miles said softly. "To

77
00:08:29.644 --> 00:08:34.523
London then!" Edward commanded. And off the two friends went, hobbling together down the roadway.

